## 📐 Key DAX Measures

```dax
// 1. Total Active Headcount
Active Headcount = 
CALCULATE(
    COUNTROWS(Dim_Employee),
    FILTER(Dim_Employee, ISBLANK(Dim_Employee[TerminationDate]) || Dim_Employee[TerminationDate] > MAX(Dim_Date[Date]))
)

// 2. Annualized Rolling Attrition Rate (%)
Rolling Attrition Rate = 
VAR TotalExits = CALCULATE(COUNTROWS(Fact_Terminations), USERELATIONSHIP(Fact_Terminations[ExitDate], Dim_Date[Date]))
VAR AvgHeadcount = ([Active Headcount] + [Beginning Headcount]) / 2
RETURN
DIVIDE(TotalExits, AvgHeadcount, 0)

// 3. Early Churn Rate (< 1 Year)
First Year Churn % = 
DIVIDE(
    CALCULATE(COUNTROWS(Fact_Terminations), Fact_Terminations[TenureMonths] <= 12),
    COUNTROWS(Fact_Terminations),
    0
)
💡 Key Business Takeaways
Month 14 Cliff: Tech attrition peaks right after Month 12 stock vesting cliffs. Recommended solution: Retention bonus / refresher equity.
Overtime & Commute Burden: Employees with >10 hrs/week overtime and >25 miles commute have a 3.8x flight risk.
